usbip-win2 -- https://github.com/vadimgrn/usbip-win2

No usbip-win2 code or header is part of this project's source; its public
headers documented the USB/IP wire format that emulator/ds5emu/wire.py
implements independently. usbip-win2 is licensed under the 2-Clause BSD
License as of release 0.9.7.0 and later (earlier releases were GPL-3.0); this
project targets 0.9.7.7.

Each release publishes one Windows installer.

ds5bridge-setup-<version>-bundled.exe embeds, unmodified and byte-for-byte,
the official installers USBip-0.9.7.7-x64.exe (usbip-win2,
BSD-2-Clause, (c) 2021-2026 Vadym Hrynchyshyn) and HidHide_1.5.230_x64.exe
(HidHide, MIT, (c) 2020 Eric Korff de Gidts, (c) 2021-2024 Benjamin
Hoeglinger-Stelzer / Nefarius Software Solutions e.U.), each installed as a
separate product under its own licence. The vendors' copyright and licence
notices are reproduced in app/packaging/bundle/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt, which
that installer places next to the uninstaller in %LOCALAPPDATA%\ds5bridge, as
the BSD-2-Clause licence requires for binary redistribution. Neither project
endorses ds5bridge.

scripts/install.ps1 redistributes nothing itself: it downloads that installer
from this project's release page and verifies its SHA-256 before running it.
A download-mode build of the installer, ds5bridge-setup-<version>.exe (built
locally with app/packaging/build-installer.ps1 without -Bundle; not
published), embeds neither package and instead downloads each vendor's
official installer from its own release page, verifying its SHA-256 first.

